From: Rex Lu <rex.lu@mediatek.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Jun 2024 10:30:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_wed: debugfs: fix the HIFTXD MSDU counter
 offsets

The A-MSDU engine has two sets of 13 HIFTXD fetch counters: the buffer
counters at 0x1e90-0x1ec0 and, right after them, the MSDU counters at
0x1ec4-0x1ef4. wed_amsdu_show() prints the MSDU counters as
MTK_WED_MON_AMSDU_HIFTXD_FETCH_MSDU(1) to (13), but the macro adds n * 4
to 0x1ec4, so the dump skips the first counter and reads 0x1ef8, past
the last one.

Number the counters from 1 in the macro, as its callers do.

Fixes: 3f3de094e834 ("net: ethernet: mtk_wed: debugfs: add WED 3.0 debugfs entries")
Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/blob/08196fa6e5d338ce88aa0002f781e2d24289b1f1/25.12/files/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12/999-wed-08-extended-wed-debugfs.patch
[plcharriere: offset fix only, with the macro argument in parentheses]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed_regs.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed_regs.h
@@ -821,7 +821,7 @@
 #define MTK_WED_AMSDU_QMEM_TID6_QTAIL			GENMASK(27, 16)
 #define MTK_WED_AMSDU_QMEM_TID7_QTAIL			GENMASK(11, 0)
 
-#define MTK_WED_MON_AMSDU_HIFTXD_FETCH_MSDU(_n)		(0x1ec4 + (_n) * 0x4)
+#define MTK_WED_MON_AMSDU_HIFTXD_FETCH_MSDU(_n)		(0x1ec4 + ((_n) - 1) * 0x4)
 
 #define MTK_WED_AMSDU_DBG_CFG				0x1fe0
 #define MTK_WED_AMSDU_DBG_CFG_EN			BIT(18)
